    <Cell ss:StyleID="Header"><Data ss:Type="String">Memory End Offset</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="Header"><Data ss:Type="String">Remarks</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="Header"><Data ss:Type="String">Test Steps / Procedure</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="Header"><Data ss:Type="String">Impacted Registers</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="Header"><Data ss:Type="String">Validation / Acceptance Criteria</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="Header"><Data ss:Type="String">Code Generation</Data></Cell>
   </Row>
   <Row ss:AutoFitHeight="1">
    <Cell ss:StyleID="DataCell"><Data ss:Type="Number">1</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="DataCell"><Data ss:Type="String">GPIO</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="DataCell"><Data ss:Type="String">Register Read Write Validation</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="DataCell"><Data ss:Type="String">gpio_reg_wr_rd_test</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="DataCell"><Data ss:Type="String">This test validates the GPIO register block by performing default value verification and write-read-back checks across all 49 GPIO registers (gp0_gpio_8 through gp0_gpio_39, interrupt raw status/clear, interrupt enable, interrupt status, IO control group, data output group, and data input group registers). Phase 1 reads each register after reset and verifies the value matches the expected default. Phase 2 writes six different bit patterns to each writable register, reads back the value, and verifies correctness using read and write masks. Certain registers with VRRW type fields at offsets 0x80 and 0x94-0xB0 are selectively skipped during write-read validation. Group registers at offsets 0x94-0xC0 are skipped during default value checks. Bit 0 (data_in) is masked during default value comparison due to its dependency on external pin state. The soft reset function is disabled in the source code.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="DataCell"><Data ss:Type="String">NA</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="DataCell"><Data ss:Type="String">NA</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="DataCell"><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="DataCell"><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="DataCell"><Data ss:Type="String">The test covers 49 registers in the gp0 register block spanning offsets 0x00 to 0xC0. Registers with VRRW type fields are selectively skipped during write-read validation. Group registers are skipped during default value checks. Bit 0 (data_in) is masked during default value comparison. The soft reset function is disabled in the source code.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="DataCell"><Data ss:Type="String">1. Initialize the GPIO register block and ensure all registers are in their post-reset state.&#10;2. Read each of the 49 GPIO registers and verify the read value (with bit 0 masked) matches the expected default reset value. Skip registers flagged in the reset-skip array.&#10;3. Skip registers that have a zero read mask.&#10;4. Record any default value mismatches as failures.&#10;5. For each of the six test patterns, write-read-compare.&#10;6. Verify PASS/FAIL.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="DataCell"><Data ss:Type="String">gp0_gpio_8; gp0_gpio_9; gp0_gpio_10</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="DataCell"><Data ss:Type="String">All 49 GPIO registers must return their expected default values after reset. All writable registers must correctly store and return six different test patterns when masked with their respective write and read masks. The test must exit with code 0 (pass) when all checks succeed.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="DataCell"><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
   </Row>
  </Table>
