   <ActivePane>2</ActivePane>
  </WorksheetOptions>
 </Worksheet>
 <Worksheet ss:Name="MetaData">
  <Table ss:DefaultColumnWidth="120" ss:DefaultRowHeight="15">
   <Column ss:Index="1" ss:AutoFitWidth="1" ss:Width="50"/>
   <Column ss:Index="2" ss:AutoFitWidth="1" ss:Width="180"/>
   <Column ss:Index="3" ss:AutoFitWidth="1" ss:Width="500"/>
   <Column ss:Index="4" ss:AutoFitWidth="1" ss:Width="500"/>
   <Column ss:Index="5" ss:AutoFitWidth="1" ss:Width="300"/>
   <Column ss:Index="6" ss:AutoFitWidth="1" ss:Width="350"/>
   <Column ss:Index="7" ss:AutoFitWidth="1" ss:Width="300"/>
   <Column ss:Index="8" ss:AutoFitWidth="1" ss:Width="300"/>
   <Column ss:Index="9" ss:AutoFitWidth="1" ss:Width="300"/>
   <Row ss:Height="30">
    <Cell ss:StyleID="Header"><Data ss:Type="String">Index</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="Header"><Data ss:Type="String">Test Case Name</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="Header"><Data ss:Type="String">Meta Test Description</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="Header"><Data ss:Type="String">Meta Test Steps / Procedure</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="Header"><Data ss:Type="String">Meta Impacted Registers</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="Header"><Data ss:Type="String">Meta Validation / Acceptance Criteria</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="Header"><Data ss:Type="String">Meta Headers</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="Header"><Data ss:Type="String">Meta Macros</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="Header"><Data ss:Type="String">Meta Arrays</Data></Cell>
   </Row>
   <Row ss:AutoFitHeight="1">
    <Cell ss:StyleID="DataCell"><Data ss:Type="Number">1</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="DataCell"><Data ss:Type="String">gpio_reg_wr_rd_test</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="DataCell"><Data ss:Type="String">This testcase validates the GPIO register block (gp0) by performing two phases: (1) Default value check (chk_rst_val): Iterates over all 49 registers in addr_array[] using MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8 through MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_10 (and 46 additional registers). For each register, if skip_rst_array[i]==1 the register is skipped, if read_mask_array[i]==0x00000000 the register is skipped. Otherwise, read_reg(addr) is called, the result is masked with 0xFFFFFFFE (clearing bit 0), and compared against default_value_array[i]. Mismatch increments def_fail_cnt. (2) Write-Read check (chk_rd_wr): Iterates over 6 test patterns {0xFFFFFFFF, 0xAAAAAAAA, 0x55555555, 0xF5F5F5F5, 0xA5A5A5A5, 0xFFFF0000}. For each pattern, writes (data_wr &amp; write_mask_array[i]) to each register (skipping if skip_array[i]==1 or write_mask_array[i]==0x00000000), then reads back (read_reg(addr) &amp; read_mask_array[i]) and compares against expected value computed as ((data_wr &amp; read_mask_array[i] &amp; write_mask_array[i]) | (wr_n &amp; read_mask_array[i] &amp; default_value_array[i])) where wr_n = (write_mask_array[i] ^ 0xFFFFFFFF). Mismatch increments wr_fail_cnt. Test passes (finish(0)) if both fail counters are zero, otherwise fails (finish(1)). soft_reset_chk() is defined but disabled via #ifdef 0. SOFT_RST_REG_ADDRESS is ignored per instructions.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="DataCell"><Data ss:Type="String">1. Include headers: stdio.h, stdlib.h, test_common.h, test_define.c.&#10;2. Define SOFT_RST_REG_ADDRESS=0x00000000 and SOFT_RST_REG_DATA=0x00000000 (unused, ignored).&#10;3. Define CNT=49, addr_array[49] with macros: {MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8, MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_9, MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_10, ...} (49 entries).&#10;4. Define default_value_array[49] with macros.&#10;5. Define read_mask_array[49] with macros.&#10;6. Define write_mask_array[49] with macros.&#10;7. Define skip_array[49]: index 32 and indices 37-44 set to 1.&#10;8. Define skip_rst_array[49]: indices 37-48 set to 1.&#10;9. Call chk_rst_val(): for each register, read and compare against default.&#10;10. Call chk_rd_wr(): for 6 patterns, write-read-compare.&#10;11. if def_fail_cnt > 0 || wr_fail_cnt > 0: finish(1) else finish(0)</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="DataCell"><Data ss:Type="String">MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8; MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_9; MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_10</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="DataCell"><Data ss:Type="String">All 49 GPIO registers must return their expected default values after reset. All writable registers must correctly store and return six different test patterns when masked with their respective write and read masks. The test must exit with code 0 (pass) when all checks succeed.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="DataCell"><Data ss:Type="String">stdio.h; stdlib.h; test_common.h; gpio/gpio_def.h; gpio/gpio_offset.h</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="DataCell"><Data ss:Type="String">CNT=49; SOFT_RST_REG_ADDRESS=0x00000000 (ignored); SOFT_RST_REG_DATA=0x00000000 (ignored)</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="DataCell"><Data ss:Type="String">test_patterns: [0xFFFFFFFF, 0xAAAAAAAA, 0x55555555, 0xF5F5F5F5, 0xA5A5A5A5, 0xFFFF0000]; skip_array: Index 32 and indices 37-44 set to 1; skip_rst_array: Indices 37-48 set to 1</Data></Cell>
   </Row>
  </Table>
